new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..1af739df66589ae698dbf4012a4134ec92a2465c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/ui/src/task-output-copy/CONTRACT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Task output complete-copy boundary
+
+- Module: `task-output-copy-ui`; layer: `ui`; owner: UI tool presentation.
+- Public entry: `contract.ts`; dependencies: `ui` (Button, IntlProvider, presentation capabilities), React and lucide-react. No new host/service path.
+- Renderer supplies tool identity, task id, raw output, truncation, copy source and execution admission. `useTaskOutputCopyAction` returns only the summary adornment; upstream status/output rendering stays in the renderer.
+- One owner: the hook owns transient busy/result state and generation; the existing capability provider owns host access. No cache or persistence.
+- Click admission precedes host reads; read exact 256 KiB ranges (maximum 8 MiB), probe EOF, decode fatal UTF-8, then copy. WebKit ClipboardItem admission remains inside the original gesture. Inline fallback requires a complete matching non-agent envelope.
+- Identity/source changes and unmount invalidate stale work; duplicate clicks are ignored. No retries, resume or replay. Desktop and Web use the same presentation hook; readonly capabilities prohibit host reads, while verified inline text remains copyable. Failures retain the existing unavailable/loading/copied/failed labels.
+- Regression evidence: contract tests cover exact ranges/EOF/staleness/UTF-8 and envelope eligibility; existing message task control tests and browser tool presentation fixture remain applicable.
