@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# tool-live-expansion
+
+## Scope and entry
+
+UI-only expansion policy for single edit and single command cards. Public entry: `contract.ts`; layer: `ui`; no runtime dependencies. ToolLayout remains the sole owner of remembered user choices. Renderers opt in with `expandWhileRunning`; Explore, executeGroup and work-process cards do not opt in.
+
+## Behavior
+
+A remembered manual choice wins over the running default. Without a choice, an opted-in running card is expanded, including when a pending card starts running. On completion the running default disappears, restoring the existing completed default. Manual expansion/collapse survives streaming updates, completion and remount. Existing forceOpen, canToggle, autoOpen and summary-action gates remain unchanged. This policy never persists a running default as a user choice.
+
+## Boundaries and regression evidence
+
+Inputs are remembered open state, running state and explicit opt-in; output is the resolved boolean. No services, IO, connection state or session storage. Tests cover the truth table and real single edit/command renderers; browser evidence uses the existing ToolLayout fixture harness with actual renderers.
+
+The companion MCP regression removes the diagnostic dialog's configuration Switch: opening/refreshing remains status-only, explicit connection checks reuse the existing list/connect path, and settings navigation and redacted copying remain available. No new connection or authorization owner is introduced.
+
+Codex status projection keeps provider/service generation isolation and adds latest-request-wins ordering within that scope. Starting cancel/disconnect invalidates in-flight status reads; their completion reloads through the existing Host service. Late success/error from an older status request cannot replace the newer accepted projection. Host remains the sole flow/token owner; sequence numbers are local to the mounted hook and are not persisted or replayed. Desktop uses the same live polling; mobile still cannot access Host authorization state.
